@baseUrl = https://localhost:7127
# Replace with the current Visual Studio HTTPS origin if different.
# Copy only the token from the creation response into this local variable.
@token = paste-token-here

### Default: omit expiresInSeconds to use 300 seconds
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/dev/teacher-grants
Content-Type: application/json

{}

### Five-minute grant
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/dev/teacher-grants
Content-Type: application/json

{ "expiresInSeconds": 300 }

### Fast expiry: open returned URL, wait at least two seconds, open again
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/dev/teacher-grants
Content-Type: application/json

{ "expiresInSeconds": 1 }

### Invalid range: expect 400 and errors.expiresInSeconds or Errors.ExpiresInSeconds
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/dev/teacher-grants
Content-Type: application/json

{ "expiresInSeconds": 3601 }

### Valid token: 200, two questions, no submit button, no-store
GET {{baseUrl}}/teacher/test-form?token={{token}}

### Extra parameters must not change the fixed fixture
GET {{baseUrl}}/teacher/test-form?token={{token}}&caseId=other&formId=other&taskId=other

### Missing token: 404, generic message, no questions
GET {{baseUrl}}/teacher/test-form

### Invalid token: 404, generic message, no token reflected
GET {{baseUrl}}/teacher/test-form?token=invalid

# Also alter one character of a real token: expect 404.
# Restart the Development process: the old token must return 404.
# Start with Production (without Development launch profile): both routes must
# return 404, including POST with malformed JSON. Never paste real tokens into Git.
